# The sun visor: a grip on the front of the helmet with the hand drawn down lowers the sun visor over the glass (the view
# darkens), and pushed up raises it again.
# Needs: Earth Planet; Options > VR > Display > Helmet view on (the default). The test closes the helmet: the sun visor rides
# on its glass, and Earth Planet starts with it open.
# The hand is placed from the head: 13 cm ahead of the eyes is on the front of the helmet (it reaches 26 cm from its middle,
# 9 cm behind the eyes) and clear of the headset (a hand within 10 cm of the eyes is dropped as not tracked); a draw of
# 5 cm slides the visor.
plugin SpaceEngineersVR
world game:Earth Planet
log SpaceEngineersVR.log
expect session focused within 60
helmet on
read character
expect helmet == true within 5

head 0 1.6 0
wait 2

# the game's exposure moves the whole view for a while after a load: the images below are compared once it has settled
expect headset steady
# before: nothing gripped, the view holds still
headset visor-a.png
wait 1
headset visor-b.png
expect headset same
expect no log Sun visor: Right hand

# the right hand to the front of the helmet, grip, drawn down 10 cm: the sun visor comes down and the view darkens
hand right 0 1.6 -0.13
wait 0.7
press right grip
wait 0.5
hand right 0 1.55 -0.13
wait 0.2
hand right 0 1.5 -0.13
wait 1.5
headset visor-down.png
expect headset changed
expect log Sun visor: Right hand on the front of the helmet drew it down within 5
expect no log the helmet is open and the visor rides on its glass

# pushed back up 10 cm: the sun visor goes up and the view lightens again
hand right 0 1.55 -0.13
wait 0.2
hand right 0 1.6 -0.13
wait 0.2
hand right 0 1.65 -0.13
wait 1.5
headset visor-up.png
expect headset changed
expect log Sun visor: Right hand on the front of the helmet pushed it up within 5
release right grip
